{"kind": "PRE_REGISTRATION", "strategy": "NQ Scalping System (user-supplied Pine v6): EMA89 trend + pullback to EMA8/EMA21 + StochRSI reset and cross", "instrument": "NAS 15m, 206,703 bars, 2016-11-14 to 2025-10-01, byte-identical to the file used in the Donchian study", "config_from_images": {"qty": 5, "point_value": 2.0, "trend_ema": 89, "fast_ema": 8, "slow_ema": 21, "use_fallback": true, "min_pullback": 15.0, "pullback_lookback": 10, "rsi_len": 14, "stoch_len": 14, "k_smooth": 3, "d_smooth": 3, "oversold": 20, "overbought": 80, "reset_lookback": 8, "use_volume": false, "use_macd": false, "session_chicago": "06:00-11:30 with 1 min warmup = 07:01-12:30 New York", "atr_len": 14, "atr_stop": 1.5, "atr_target": 2.5, "use_trail": true, "trail_always_fixed_points": true, "trail_arm": 15.0, "trail_offset": 8.0, "early_exits": "all off", "quick_scalp": "off", "commission": "1.24 cash per contract per order", "slippage": "1 tick"}, "note_no_flatten": "The Pine gates ENTRIES by session but has no session exit, so a position can run for days. Both variants are measured.", "intrabar_problem": "The trailing stop (arm 15 pts, offset 8 pts) is path-dependent and the median hold is 1 bar. A 15m OHLC file cannot order prices inside a bar, so every headline is bracketed under three exit conventions: intrabar-favorable, intrabar-adverse, and barclose (trail may only arm or tighten from CLOSED bars).", "primary_model": "trail_mode=barclose, order=adverse. It makes no claim a 15m file cannot support. intrabar is reported as the optimistic bracket, not as the result.", "split": "first 65% of sessions research, last 35% holdout, chronological on sessions", "holdout_status": "This NAS holdout was read twice for the Donchian study. This strategy is a different family and was specified by the user, not selected by me on this data, so it gets ONE look at the configurations declared below.", "preregistered_holdout_tests": ["as-written config, barclose/adverse", "as-written config, barclose/favorable", "as-written config, intrabar/adverse", "as-written config, intrabar/favorable", "walk-forward-selected variant (selected on research only)"], "NPRE": 5, "bonferroni_threshold": 0.01, "pass_criterion": "PASS on the holdout requires, for the primary model: (a) net expectancy > 0 after costs, AND (b) excess over the matched control with p < 0.01 (Bonferroni for NPRE=5). Reporting a PASS under the intrabar convention alone is explicitly NOT a pass.", "prior": "Trail-off expectancy is already negative on the full sample (-1.11 to -2.09 pts/trade), and random entries pushed through the same trailing exit earn +2.47 to +4.04 pts/trade under the intrabar convention. Prior expectation: the profit is the exit mechanic interacting with the bar model, and the signal contributes about +1 pt/trade over random, which is roughly the size of the round-turn cost. Recorded so a positive result cannot be framed as expected and a negative one cannot be framed as surprising.", "searches_allowed": "Parameter sensitivity, walk-forward re-selection and all Monte Carlo work happen on the RESEARCH block only.", "id": "N0001"}
{"kind": "PRE_REGISTRATION_AMENDMENT", "amends": "N0001", "when": "Recorded BEFORE any holdout number was produced. The holdout has not been opened for this study.", "reason": "A search over 5 session windows on the research block found that restricting to 09:30-11:00 New York (08:30-10:00 Chicago) is the only variant positive after costs under the primary path-free model. It also beats the matched control on research (excess +3.19 pts/trade, p 0.0275 at barclose/adverse). It is the single most promising thing in the study and deserves a holdout look rather than being reported as an unresolved research finding.", "multiplicity_it_carries": "Best of 5 windows searched. On research its nominal p 0.0275 becomes ~0.14 after a Bonferroni correction for those 5, so it is NOT significant on research once the search is priced in. The holdout test is what decides it.", "new_test": "6. RTH sub-window 09:30-11:00 New York, as-written parameters otherwise, barclose/adverse (primary) - the other conventions reported alongside but not counted.", "NPRE_old": 5, "NPRE_new": 6, "bonferroni_threshold_new": 0.008333333333333333, "pass_criterion_unchanged": "PASS still requires expectancy > 0 after costs AND excess over the matched control below the Bonferroni threshold, on the PRIMARY path-free model. A pass under the intrabar convention alone is explicitly not a pass.", "prior": "The research-block excess is not significant after correcting for the 5-window search, and the sub-window has only 299 research trades. Prior expectation: it does not survive.", "id": "N0002"}
